#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
#title[Identity type of dirichlet product with FTIT]

We present an alternative proof of the characterization of the identity type of the dirichlet product using the #local("00EK")[fundamental theorem of identity types].

Let $(T,U,e,a,b)$ and $(T',U',e',a',b')$ be terms in the #local("00DP")[dirichlet product] $(F
*_D G)(S)$ of #local("00DT")[species] $F$ and $G$.
Then there is an equivalence
$
  ((d,a,b) =_((F *_D G)(S)) (d',a',b'))\
  ~= sum_((f,g,alpha): "Eq-cart-dec"(S)(d, d')) ("tr"_F (tilde(f),a) = a') xx ("tr"_G (tilde(g),b) = b')
$

